    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d874">

                <pb facs="1092" n="1082" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1082"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/2–2647</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chinese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Koo</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the Chinese
                    Ambassador and has the honor to refer to this Government’s agreement with the
                    Government of China on the Principles Applying to Mutual Aid, signed June 2,
                        1942,<anchor n="96" xml:id="d874-f1"/> and to article 7.d. of the agreement
                    of the two Governments for the Sale of Certain Surplus War Property, signed
                    August 30, 1946, and proposes the initiation in Washington on or before April
                    15, 1947 of negotiations for the final settlement of war accounts outstanding
                    between the two Governments, including obligations of both Governments under the
                    Mutual Aid Agreement. It is proposed that the Chinese Government at its earliest
                    convenience designate the persons who will represent it in these
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-26">February 26,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
